{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"1. Compilation errors fixed:\n- `mvn ... -DskipTests clean compile` now passes (exit code `0`), so the codebase compiles after the fix.\n- I applied a focused fix for the multipart regression that came from the refactor: `TestRequest` was importing jsoup’s moved `Attribute` class instead of Netty’s multipart `Attribute`, which prevented multipart form fields from being added to request parameters.\n\n2. Files changed:\n- [TestRequest.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/test/java/org/jsoup/integration/netty/TestRequest.java)\n\n3. Original refactoring goal preserved:\n- Yes. I did not revert package restructuring in `org.jsoup.nodes` or move classes back.\n- The change is a minimal import-level correction aligned with the refactored package layout.\n\n4. Remaining risks:\n- Full `clean verify` is currently blocked in this environment by Netty server socket restrictions (`java.net.SocketException: Operation not permitted`), causing integration test setup failures unrelated to compilation.\n- Because of that environment limit, I could not fully re-run the previously failing multipart integration assertions end-to-end here, but the root cause in code was corrected."}}
